title: Dealing with Toleration
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/portraits/AskewHeinrich.jpg
view-if: dealing_with_toleration_timer = 0 and marcher_toleration and chancellor_party == "Unionist" and concord_formed
on-arrival: dealing_with_toleration_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs
#subtitle: Despite not being in government, we can still provide support.

= Dealing with Toleration

We are currently providing external support to the government of Chancellor [+ chancellor +], but our influence has been severely weakened due to the formation of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> by former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> members. Furthermore, the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> is actively trying to distance itself from our support. How should we use our position?

- @break_toleration
- @urge_against_austerity_limited
- @improve_relations
- @stay_course: Stay the course, for stability's sake.
- @easy_discard

@break_toleration
view-if: not constructive_vonc
title: End the toleration agreement with a vote of no confidence!

Are we sure about this? A vote of no confidence would trigger new elections, and potentially an increased vote-share for the extremist parties. [? if in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] also threatens a no-confidence vote against us in Heartland, pressuring us to stay the course.?]

- @vonc: Yes, end this arrangement!
- @stay_course: No, we should stay the course.

@vonc
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; left_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 5; burgher_marcher -= 3; landed_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; faithful_marcher -= 3; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 5; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; ddp_right += 1; gold_right += 2
go-to: new_prussia_election if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and ((center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"); center_right_coalition_prussia if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and (((center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 or right_coalition_heartland >= 50) and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or bourgeois_coalition_heartland >= 50)

We have called for a vote of no confidence, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting chancellor.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; collectivist_relation += 5; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; lvp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; landed_marcher -= 2; guild_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; faithful_royalist += 2; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory vote in Heartland, forcing the dissolution of the state Assembly for new elections.

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland + 2365 +].

A double dissolution has shaken the people's faith in democracy, with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that the Commonwealth needs a strong leader.

@center_right_coalition_prussia
on-arrival: in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 1; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; burgher_marcher -= 3; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.06; heartland_police_strength -= 8; 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory no confidence vote in Heartland, replacing our government with a center-right coalition composed of all parties to our right, except for the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. While this is a setback, it is not the worst possible outcome, as new elections could have led to significant gains for extremist parties.

[? if unionist_leader != "Sedgewick": Adam Sedgewick?][? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": Edmund Askew?] of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is selected to be the Minister-President of Heartland.

@urge_failure
on-arrival: gold_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; concord_left += 1; commons_unionist -= 2; commons_marcher += 2; disfavored_unionist -= 2; disfavored_marcher += 2

Unfortunately, the historically strict party discipline of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> has carried over to its successor, which has successfully rallied the party against the bill. However, this is sure to spark discontent within the party, as it struggles to maintain its diverse coalition while also attempting to implement its fiscal reform policy.

@urge_against_austerity_limited
title: Put forth a proposal to increase welfare spending and reverse austerity cuts.
subtitle: This move will drive a wedge between the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> and their Labor and <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> factions.
go-to: urge_success_limited if unionist_relation >= 40; urge_failure if unionist_relation < 40

@urge_success_limited
on-arrival: bruning_austerity_limited += 1; commons_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher += 3*(1-dissent) if bruning_austerity_limited >= 3; burgher_ddp += 2; guild_ddp += 2; burgher_gold += 2; guild_gold += 2; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; burgher_lvp += 2; guild_lvp += 2; unionist_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 5; gold_right += 1; ddp_right += 0.5; lvp_right += 1; dufour_angry_bruning += 10; economic_growth += 0.2; disfavored -= 0.2; concord_left += 2

The motion passes! Despite the historically strict party discipline within the former <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, the diverse base of the party has weakened the leadership’s control over its parliamentary delegation. However, this has left the incumbent cabinet vulnerable to strong attacks from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #003755;">right</span>, as it further cements their association with the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> in the eyes of their industrial backers.

[? if bruning_austerity_limited == 1: We have successfully prevented Askew from decreasing taxes on high earners, thus lessening the burden of compensatory tax increases on the lower strata. ?][? if bruning_austerity_limited == 2: We have successfully pressured Askew into appeasing us by reinstating the 40-hour workweek, although wages remain suboptimal. ?][? if bruning_austerity_limited >= 3: We have successfully pressured Askew into reversing some salary cuts for civil servants. ?]

@improve_relations
title: Improve relations with the parties of the coalition.
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 4*(1-dissent); gold_relation += 3*(1-dissent); ddp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); lvp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); left_dissent += 5; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 0.5; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; lvp_left += 1; traditionalist_angry += 1 if marcher_toleration_right

We have increased our level of contact and discussions with the parties of the coalition, primarily the [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist:and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed:and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] and, to some extent, the <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>. However, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> elements of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span> continue to obstruct our efforts to foster constructive cooperation with Askew.

Our attempts to reach out to the center-right are met with disdain from the leftists within our party.

@stay_course

We will stay the course of toleration, for the sake of stability.
